<title>CANADA: Foreigners sell Canada securities in March.</title>
<headline>Foreigners sell Canada securities in March.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign investors sold a net C$2.144 billion in Canadian securities in March, after buying a net C$1.28 billion in February (revised from C$1.13 billion), Statistics Canada said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Canadian residents bought a net C$2.109 billion of foreign securities after buying C$608 million in February (revised from C$572 million).</p>
<p>Foreign investments in Canadian securities (blns of dollars):</p>
<p>				 Mar	Feb	Year to date</p>
<p>    Total		   -2.144   +1.283    +3.868</p>
<p>    Bonds		   -1.351   +0.676    +1.428</p>
<p>    Money mkt paper     +0.098   +1.032    +3.182</p>
<p>    Stocks		  -0.891   -0.424    -0.742</p>
<p>Canadian investment in foreign securities (blns of dollars):</p>
<p>				  Mar	Feb     Year to date</p>
<p>    Total		   -2.109   -0.608    -4.536</p>
<p>    Bonds		   -1.277   +0.274    -1.189</p>
<p>    Stocks		  -0.831   -0.882    -3.347</p>
<p>(A minus sign indicates more purchases from than sales of securities to non-residents, i.e. an outflow of money from Canada, Statistics Canada said.)</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Balance of Payments Division, Don Granger at 613-951-1864.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
